CREATED:20260501T213652Z
DESCRIPTION:ADF Debut\nProgram: Dirty Laundry\nRunning time: 65 minutes\, 
 no intermission\nTickets: $30\nTickets are purchased through Duke Univers
 ity's Box Office.\n\nPost-Performance Discussion\n\n\nCompany Website: ht
 tps://www.lcpdance.com/\n\nDirty Laundry is a multimedia and multi-layere
 d dance work by director/choreographer Li Chiao-Ping\, composer Byron Au 
 Yong\, and visual artist Hong Huo that investigates the history of Chines
 e labor\, systemic racism\, and generational trauma through a balance of 
 expressive choreography\, visual imagery\, spoken word\, text\, and sound
 scapes. It tells the untold stories of struggle and survival that charact
 erized the Asian experience in America-the institutionalized violence and
  the treatment of Asians as perpetual foreigners. Dancers bring their per
 sonal histories to life on stage\, creating a vivid tapestry of resilienc
 e\, pain\, and humanity that transforms into a shared\, communal act of r
 emembrance and healing.\n\nPhoto Credit: Mats Rudels\n_________\n\nADF of
 fers a 20% discount to Duke employees and $20 tickets to Duke students (r
 estrictions apply). To access your discount\, just log in with your Duke 
 Net ID at tickets.duke.edu.
DURATION:PT1H5M
DTSTAMP:20260501T213652Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T193000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T213652Z
