CREATED:20260501T214145Z
DESCRIPTION:Program: On the Nature of Things\, Virtuous & Vicious\, Lament
 ation Variations\, Nocturne\, Day Two\nRunning time: 115 minutes\, includ
 ing one intermission\nTickets: $40-$70\nTickets are purchased through Duk
 e University's Box Office.\n\nPost-Performance Discussion on Friday\, Jul
 y 24 at 7:30 pm.\n\nCompany Websites: pilobolus.org\n\nPilobolus brings a
  new work\, Virtuous & Vicious\, and some classics to ADF this summer. Th
 e company celebrates the centennial anniversary of the Martha Graham Danc
 e Company with Lamentation Variations Project\, an interpretation of Grah
 am's seminal work\, Lamentation. The thematic richness of On the Nature o
 f Things draws from a tapestry of intellectual\, historical\, and artisti
 c sources\, specifically the philosophies and works of Da Vinci\, Milton\
 , Vivaldi\, and Stravinsky. Nocturne explores how real-life noises infect
  dreams and vice versa. Day Two is a classic\, high-energy piece that dep
 icts the second day of the creation of the world.\n\nPhoto Credit: Mahaiw
 e\n_________\n\nADF offers a 20% discount to Duke employees and $20 ticke
 ts to Duke students (restrictions apply). To access your discount\, just 
 log in with your Duke Net ID at tickets.duke.edu.
DURATION:PT1H55M
DTSTAMP:20260501T214145Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260724T193000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T214145Z
